<title>USA: Motorola, Rockwell in alliance.</title>
<headline>Motorola, Rockwell in alliance.</headline>
<dateline>HUNTSVILLE, Ala. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Information Systems Group and Rockwell International Corp unit Rockwell Semiconductor Systems Thursday said they plan to jointly develop K56, establishing the benchmark in 56K modem technology.</p>
<p>Motorola said it expects to introduce modems in early March based on Rockwell's K56 technology.</p>
<p>The partnership promotes rapid development of 56K standards and assures that once they are adopted, customers will fully benefit with increased performance, Motorola said.</p>
</text>
